WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.000
Unless you’ve been living under the rock the past&nbsp;
few years it is very likely you use Software as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.480
Service, or SaaS, on a daily basis for business&nbsp;
and as a consumer. SaaS is one of the three main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:16.480
categories of cloud computing, Infrastructure as&nbsp;
a Service, or IaaS, and Platform as a Service,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:22.640
or PaaS. Out of the big 3 cloud computing models,&nbsp;
SaaS is the most popular and commonly used one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.200
AND the great thing about it is you don’t have&nbsp;
to be a developer or an IT expert to use it!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:34.640
So, SaaS in a nutshell is a method of delivering&nbsp;
software and applications over the internet via a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:40.560
subscription model. This a game changer compared&nbsp;
to our traditional software model used prior to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.120
the emergence of cloud computing, where users&nbsp;
would have to manage, install, and upgrade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.960
software themselves on local servers or computers.&nbsp;
With SaaS you can simply provision a server for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:55.760
an instance in cloud, and in a couple of hours,&nbsp;
you’ll have your software or application ready for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:02.880
use. Some key examples would be the email client&nbsp;
you use such as GMail, the applications and tools&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:08.080
you have on your computer, such as Microsoft&nbsp;
Office 365 or Adobe Creative Cloud, or even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:13.040
when you are jamming out to your favorite music&nbsp;
streaming service, these are all SaaS, providing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:19.200
productivity apps over the internet. SaaS is also&nbsp;
used in a wide variety of business operations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:26.560
today, such as communication and collaboration,&nbsp;
customer relationship management, billing, sales&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:32.000
management, human resources management, financial&nbsp;
management, enterprise resourcing planning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.720
you get the gist, the list goes on and on. So,&nbsp;
unlike our other cloud computing service models,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:43.200
SaaS is the very top of the IT stack and has the&nbsp;
highest level of abstraction. So, this means the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.280
cloud service provider will be providing and&nbsp;
maintaining all these layers for you in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:52.240
stack. So, let's take a look what that might look&nbsp;
like and see how a user would typically consume a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:57.520
SaaS application. So I'm just going to go ahead&nbsp;
and just shift these other stacks over here and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:05.680
let's slide the SaaS deck right here. Okay. So,&nbsp;
our users would access a SaaS application within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:12.560
what we call a multi-tenant architecture, and by&nbsp;
tenant I mean user. So, you'd have multiple users&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:18.640
all accessing the same pool of resources within&nbsp;
the stack. So it'd be the same hosted environment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:24.960
same hosted servers where multiple users would&nbsp;
have their own dedicated space to securely store&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:30.240
their data. There's a lot of benefits with this in&nbsp;
a SaaS application. So let's take a look at a few.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:37.840
So one you know right off the bat is it's much&nbsp;
more cost efficient compared to our other models&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.560
because again, which is the overall theme of this&nbsp;
whole video, is cloud service providers would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.120
maintaining and managing the application&nbsp;
for you. So, there's no IT overhead cost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:54.160
and a SaaS application is typically consumed on&nbsp;
a subscription-based model which is either on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.160 --> 00:03:00.880
an annual basis or a monthly basis. And&nbsp;
that includes support typically whereas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:06.240
with our older traditional models, on-prem, you&nbsp;
would have a perpetual license where you'd have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:11.120
a pretty large up front cost and then you'd&nbsp;
have to pay for support on going separately.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:21.600
Two, scalability, right. So, you can horizontally&nbsp;
or vertically scale on demand because again that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.600
cloud service provider is going to be maintaining&nbsp;
everything for you. So if you need to add more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:31.840
databases, or you need more compute power they'll&nbsp;
take care of that for you on a has needed basis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:38.720
Another benefit is you can access your&nbsp;
SaaS application anywhere which is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:42.560
huge benefit right now especially if you&nbsp;
want to mobilize your workforce, right. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:48.320
all you need is a web browser and internet&nbsp;
connectivity to be up and running with your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:52.960
SaaS application. There's no installation,&nbsp;
there's typically no plugins involved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:57.120
and you can no matter where you reside&nbsp;
geographically, you can always be up and running.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:03.360
Now I should say if you are looking for a SaaS&nbsp;
solution there are some instances where you do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:09.680
need to keep your data in the same location where&nbsp;
you reside. For instance, with Europe we have GDPR&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:14.720
and by law you have to maintain your data&nbsp;
where you reside. So, there are going to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:21.360
some instances like that, but for the most&nbsp;
part SaaS is a highly secure solution. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:30.000
then last but not least, you always have a new&nbsp;
version, right. So, once again there's no need to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:36.960
update your licensing or update manually the new&nbsp;
version of your software because that's all taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:42.000
care for you and it's automatically upgraded.&nbsp;
And this helps with a lot of wide range of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.280
issues typically if there's version control,&nbsp;
right. In the past you'd download software&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.520
and then you might be operating with something&nbsp;
that's not compatible with a different version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:56.640
of that software. So, everyone's on the same&nbsp;
version of that software and you don't have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:01.280
manually update and worry about patching and all&nbsp;
that junk, everything's taken care of for you. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:06.400
this is just a very quick overview of&nbsp;
Software as a Service. Thank you for joining.&nbsp;&nbsp;

